  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Limited to 5 prop gestures, it would be nice to be able to add buttons with triggers on our avatars that can act out the same scripts as the gestures do. For instance - i program a cube button on my avatar's neck when pressed toggles my helmet on/off, or a gun at my side when clicked triggers the gun to be in my hand which is itself a button and when trigger-pulled shoots. Theres endless possibilities, it just allows so many more animations than the 5 we are limited to. Also a bonus feature: being able to set the button to private for only you to use, or public for others to interact with - to go along with the \"chairs on avatars\" future thing planned (you KNOW someone's gonna make a mech suit with chair, why not throw a public \"fire turret\" button in there.)",
